  "caveats": [
    "The same-host result supports a clear full-navigation win for this bounded RSC candidate, but it does not isolate RSC as the sole cause: the RSC route intentionally skips the legacy application bundle and third-party analytics while the Inertia route loads them.",
    "Product LCP improves modestly. Discover LCP is directionally better but noisier: two of sixteen cycle-paired samples regressed, and the two batch medians differ materially.",
    "Response end is a tie on Product and inconclusive on Discover; it should not be claimed as an RSC win.",
    "RSC sends 80-100% more HTML while sending about half the JavaScript and no duplicated Inertia data-page payload.",
    "The run is unthrottled desktop headless Chrome, not mobile PageSpeed or field data. Live Gumroad comparisons remain diagnostic because media, chrome, caching, CDN, and third-party services are not matched.",
    "The first media-gate request received a transient 503 while the deployment woke; the exact gate passed after warm-up. Each measured run used two explicit server warmups.",
    "The harness opens the common host root before each measured target. This warms a shared connection and common resources equally, but differs from a fully cold first visit."
  ]
